---
import fs from 'node:fs';
import path from 'node:path';
const ja = Astro.props.lang === 'ja';
const proposal = 'https://github.com/matsumotory/ngx_mruby/blob/next/docs/proposals/edge-control.md';
// The proposal table owns status; the site only supplies explanatory copy.
const ledger = fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(process.cwd(), '../docs/proposals/edge-control.md'), 'utf8');
// Cells are split on unescaped pipes (GFM allows \| inside a cell), and the
// Status column is found by its header, not by its position.
const cells = line => line.split(/(?<!\\)\|/).slice(1, -1).map(cell => cell.trim());
const header = ledger.split('\n').find(line => /^\| Use case \|/.test(line));
const statusColumn = header ? cells(header).indexOf('Status') : -1;
if (statusColumn < 0) throw new Error('The use-case ledger has no Status column');
const states = new Map(ledger.split('\n').filter(line => /^\| \[.*\]\(#/.test(line)).map(line => {
  const fields = cells(line);
  const id = fields[0].match(/\]\(#([^)]*)\)/)?.[1];
  const status = fields[statusColumn]?.match(/`(designing|direction|next|2\.x)`/)?.[1];
  if (!id || !status) throw new Error('Invalid use-case ledger row');
  return [id, status];
}));
if (states.size !== ledger.split('\n').filter(line => /^\| \[.*\]\(#/.test(line)).length) {
  throw new Error('Duplicate use-case ledger id');
}
const cases = [
  { id: 'mcp-tool-authorization', status: 'designing',
    title: ['MCPツールの呼び出し権限を確認する', 'Check permissions for MCP tool calls'],
    text: ['MCPサービスの運用者が、ユーザーごとに呼び出せるMCPツールと引数の範囲を制限するための設計です。AI applicationとMCPサーバーの間にMCP gatewayを置き、認証済みユーザーの権限とtools/callの内容をRubyで照合する方法を検討しています。許可された呼び出しだけを転送し、個々のデータへのアクセス権限はMCPサーバーでも検証する構成を目指します。', 'An MCP service operator could restrict the MCP tools and argument ranges available to each user. The design places an MCP gateway between the AI application and MCP server, where Ruby would compare tools/call with the authenticated user’s permissions. Only allowed calls would be forwarded; the MCP server would still enforce access to individual data objects.'] },
  { id: 'mcp-burst-control', status: 'direction',
    title: ['MCP呼び出しの集中を制限する', 'Limit bursts of MCP calls'],
    text: ['AI applicationがMCPツールを短時間に繰り返し呼び出したり、多数のストリームを開いたりする場合に、MCPサービスの負荷を制限する構想です。Rubyで認証済みユーザーと呼び出しの種類を識別し、nginxのlimit_reqとlimit_connで設定済みの上限を適用する構成を検討します。必要な読み直しまでループと判定せず、制限時に再試行できる条件を返すことが設計上の課題です。', 'To bound load when AI applications repeatedly call MCP tools or open many streams, Ruby would identify the authenticated user and call class, and nginx limit_req and limit_conn would apply configured limits. Legitimate rereads would not be treated as loops; rejection responses would describe the conditions for retry.'] },
  { id: 'mcp-tool-profiles', status: 'designing',
    title: ['利用するAI applicationにMCPツールを合わせる', 'Select an MCP tool interface for the AI application'],
    text: ['MCPサービスの同じ処理を、異なるMCPツールの構成を必要とするAI applicationから利用するための設計です。接続プロファイルに応じてMCP gatewayがadapterを選び、adapterがtools/listとtools/callを一貫して提供する方法を検討しています。検索や取得の処理をAI applicationごとに複製せず、MCPツールの表現と呼び出し方の違いを吸収することが目的です。', 'The same MCP service could support AI applications that require different MCP tool interfaces. The design would let an MCP gateway select a versioned adapter by connection profile, with consistent tools/list and tools/call behavior. The aim is to adapt tool descriptions and calls without duplicating search and retrieval logic for each application.'] },
  { id: 'mcp-progressive-retrieval', status: 'designing',
    title: ['文書を必要な範囲から取得する', 'Retrieve the needed part of a document first'],
    text: ['agentが長い文書を一度に読み込まず、必要な箇所をMCPツールで取得し、足りなければ読み足せるようにする設計です。MCP gatewayは取得方式と処理量の上限を選び、文書の位置・版・続きを取得するための情報はバックエンドが管理する分担を検討しています。JSONやストリームを途中で切らず、範囲指定に対応した取得機能を使う構成です。', 'An agent could read the relevant passage of a long document and request more when needed instead of fetching everything at once. ngx_mruby would select a retrieval profile and processing budget; the backend would own document positions, versions and continuation information. Retrieval would use a range-aware MCP tool, not arbitrary truncation of JSON or a stream.'] },
  { id: 'mcp-next-step-guidance', status: 'direction',
    title: ['検索結果がない場合の次の手順を伝える', 'Return next steps when retrieval cannot produce a result'],
    text: ['MCPツールの検索結果がない場合や取得に失敗した場合に、agentが理由を読み、次の探索を選べる応答を返す構想です。MCP gatewayは該当なし・権限不足・取得先の障害を区別して中継し、検索対象に固有の手掛かりはMCPサービスが提供する分担を検討します。検索の意味をgatewayで変更せず、検索を続けるか、条件を変えるかの判断はagentに残す方針です。', 'When an MCP search returns no result or retrieval fails, the agent should receive the reason and available next steps. ngx_mruby would preserve the distinction between no match, denied access and an unavailable source; the MCP service would supply domain-specific guidance. The gateway would not change query meaning or promote instructions in retrieved documents into execution instructions.'] },
  { id: 'mcp-trajectory-logging', status: 'direction',
    title: ['MCPツールの呼び出し順序を観測する', 'Observe sequences of MCP tool calls'],
    text: ['MCPサービスの運用者が、agentによる検索、文書取得、再検索の流れと各処理の結果を調べる用途です。呼び出しを相関IDで関連付け、MCPツール名、成否、所要時間を記録する構想です。検索語や文書本文は標準では収集せず、保存期間と収集量に上限を設けます。調査を続けるかどうかの判断はagentに残す方針です。', 'An MCP service operator could examine the sequence and outcomes of search, document retrieval and repeated search performed by an agent. A correlation ID would connect MCP tool names, outcomes and durations. Queries and document bodies would not be collected by default, and retention and collection volume would be bounded. The agent would still decide whether to continue its investigation.'] },
  { id: 'llm-api-fallback', status: 'designing',
    title: ['model APIのエラー時に転送先を選び直す', 'Select another model API endpoint after an error'],
    text: ['各アプリにmodel APIの切替処理を実装せず、gatewayで管理する設計です。上流が429や再送対象のエラーを返した場合、Rubyで互換性のある転送先と認証情報を選び、nginxが再送する構成を検討しています。処理や課金の重複を避けるため、安全に再実行できるリクエストに限って回数と時間を制限し、応答を送り始めた後は別の生成結果につなぎ替えません。', 'Instead of implementing model API fallback separately in each application, an operator could manage it at the gateway. After an upstream 429 or another configured retryable error, Ruby would select a compatible endpoint and credentials, and nginx would retry. Attempts and time would be bounded and limited to requests safe to replay, addressing duplicate processing or charges. Once response delivery starts, another generated stream would not be spliced in.'] },
  { id: 'ai-crawler-and-bot-control', status: 'direction',
    title: ['AI crawlerやagentのアクセスを制限する', 'Control requests from AI crawlers and agents'],
    text: ['WebサイトやAPIの運用者が、AI crawlerやagentのrequestに適用する規則をRubyで選ぶ構想です。巡回による収集と、ユーザーの指示で行うアクセスを区別し、認証状態やアクセス先に応じて頻度と同時接続数を制限する設計を検討します。User-Agentの自己申告だけでverified botやsigned agentと判断せず、識別できない相手の扱いも定める必要があります。', 'A website or API operator could select Ruby policies for requests from AI crawlers and agents, distinguishing collection by a crawler from access on a user’s behalf. Authentication state and the requested resource would inform rate and concurrency limits. A User-Agent claim alone would not establish a verified bot or signed agent; treatment of unidentified clients would also need to be defined.'] },
  { id: 'semantic-cache', status: 'direction',
    title: ['外部のセマンティックキャッシュを参照する', 'Consult an external semantic cache'],
    text: ['model APIに送る内容が似たリクエストに保存済みの回答を再利用し、アプリ側の処理を変えずにmodel APIへの問い合わせを減らす構想です。gatewayがユーザーのアクセス範囲やmodelなどの条件を渡し、外部サービスが類似性と再利用の可否を判断する分担を検討します。適切な回答がない場合、判断が曖昧な場合、タイムアウト時は元のmodel APIへ転送します。回答をキャッシュへ保存する方式は未設計です。', 'An external semantic cache could reuse a stored answer for a similar model API request without changing the application. The gateway would supply constraints such as the user’s access scope and model; the external service would assess similarity and reuse validity. A miss, uncertain match or timeout would fall through to the original model API endpoint. The mechanism for storing responses in the cache is not yet designed.'] },
  { id: 'log-handler-telemetry', status: 'direction',
    title: ['logハンドラで記録した値を外部へ送る', 'Export metadata recorded by the log handler'],
    text: ['サービスの運用者が、ステータス、応答時間、転送先などを外部の集計基盤で確認するための構想です。現在のlogハンドラはネットワーク応答を待てないため、上限付きのworkerキュー、タイマー、ノンブロッキングな通信を使う送信処理を計画しています。収集先の遅延で応答を止めず、キューの満杯時や送信の失敗時の扱いを定めます。', 'A service operator could inspect status, response time and routing decisions in an external collector. The current log handler cannot wait for a network response, so export is planned through a bounded worker queue, timers and nonblocking transport. Collector delays must not stall responses; overflow and delivery-failure behavior need explicit contracts.'] },
];
// The copy of each case says 設計 or 構想 (design or direction), so a change
// of its row in the ledger stops the build until the copy is reviewed.
for (const item of cases) {
  if (states.get(item.id) !== item.status) throw new Error(`Review homepage use-case copy: ${item.id} is ${states.get(item.id)} in the ledger, ${item.status} in the copy`);
}
if (states.size !== cases.length) throw new Error('Homepage cases and proposal ledger differ');
const label = status => ja ? (status === 'designing' ? '設計中' : '構想') : (status === 'designing' ? 'Designing' : 'Direction');
---
<section class="v3-directions" aria-labelledby="directions-title">
  <div class="v3-section-heading"><h2 id="directions-title">{ja ? '今後のユースケースと設計状況' : 'Future use cases and their design status'}</h2>
    <p>{ja ? '上のmodel APIの振り分けは実行できる例です。以下では、AI applicationからMCPサーバーへの呼び出し、model APIの切替、サイトへ来るAI crawlerやagentのrequestに、nginxとRubyをどう使うかを説明します。呼び出し先の処理やagentの判断をgatewayに集めるのではなく、認可や転送、負荷の制御をどこで担うかを設計しています。「設計中」は最初の実行例と検証条件を記述した段階、「構想」は方向性を記述した段階を示します。どちらも用途全体を動かすテストはまだありません。' : 'The model API routing example above can be run today. The following designs describe uses of nginx and Ruby for MCP calls from AI applications, model API fallback, and requests arriving at a site from AI crawlers and agents. They place authorization, routing and load controls at a gateway while leaving service processing and agent decisions with their respective implementations. “Designing” means a first recipe and acceptance criteria are documented; “Direction” means the direction is documented. Neither status means a test runs the complete use case yet.'}</p>
  </div>
  <div class="direction-list">
    {cases.map(item => <article class="direction-usecase" data-use-case={item.id}>
      <div class="direction-scan"><h3>{item.title[ja ? 0 : 1]}</h3><p class="direction-status"><span class="site-badge">{label(states.get(item.id))}</span></p></div>
      <div class="direction-body"><p>{item.text[ja ? 0 : 1]}</p><a href={`${proposal}#${item.id}`}>{ja ? '設計と必要な機能を読む' : 'Read the design and required features'}</a></div>
    </article>)}
  </div>
</section>
